From: Codex <codex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mm: defer WIPEONFORK anon_vma creation until fault

Reason: upstream93949bb fixes the initial WIPEONFORK implementation. During
VMA duplication vm_prev/vm_next still refer to parent neighbors, so eager
anon_vma_prepare can incorrectly reuse the parent's anon_vma. Since no pages
are copied for this child VMA, prepare only at its first fault.
Files affected: kernel/fork.c.
Verification: compile against pinned DS-ACK; test parent preservation, child
zero fill, repeated child/grandchild forks and KEEPONFORK after a test boot.
Reference: 93949bb21b52aae924fd26f9775c8655dd9e885e.
---
--- a/kernel/fork.c
+++ b/kernel/fork.c
@@ -633,10 +633,8 @@
 			goto fail_nomem_policy;
 		tmp->vm_mm = mm;
 		if (tmp->vm_flags & VM_WIPEONFORK) {
-			/* The child sees a fresh anonymous mapping after fork. */
+			/* Prepare a fresh anon_vma lazily on the child's first fault. */
 			tmp->anon_vma = NULL;
-			if (anon_vma_prepare(tmp))
-				goto fail_nomem_anon_vma_fork;
 		} else if (anon_vma_fork(tmp, mpnt))
 			goto fail_nomem_anon_vma_fork;
 		tmp->vm_flags &=
